---
import LegalLayout from '@layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Cookie Policy for Bangladesh Travel Guide explaining current analytics cookies, how to manage cookies, and how future advertising or affiliate tracking may work."
  lastUpdated="October 26, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Cookie Policy explains how cookies and similar technologies may be used when you visit
    <a href="https://www.bangladeshtravelguide.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bangladesh Travel Guide</a>.
    Please read it together with our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What Are Cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files that a website or a third-party service may store in your browser.
    Similar technologies, such as pixels, tags, and local storage, can help websites understand how
    visitors use a site, remember settings, measure advertising, or attribute referrals.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Cookies We Currently Use</h2>
  <p>
    Bangladesh Travel Guide does not require an account, login, or shopping cart, and we do not
    intentionally use our own cookies to store personal preferences. We do not currently display
    advertisements or use affiliate links.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics to understand general website traffic and how visitors use our guides.
    Google Analytics may use cookies, including cookies with names beginning with <code>_ga</code>,
    to distinguish browsers and compile usage reports. The information may include pages visited,
    approximate geographic area, device and browser information, and interactions with the site.
    We use these reports to assess and improve our content. Cookie names, purposes, and retention
    periods may change with Google's service and configuration.
  </p>
  <p>
    For details, see Google's
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">information about cookies</a>
    and its
    <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    We also use Google Search Console to monitor our site's performance in Google Search. Search
    Console provides reports to the site owner; it does not, by itself, place cookies on your
    device through your visit to our pages.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Advertising Cookies If We Add Google AdSense</h2>
  <p>
    We do not currently display Google AdSense advertisements. If we introduce AdSense in the
    future, Google and its advertising partners may use cookies or similar technologies to deliver
    and measure ads, limit repeated ads, detect ad interactions, and, depending on the applicable
    settings and your choices, personalise advertising based on visits to this or other websites.
    The technologies used and the information processed will depend on the advertising services
    and settings in place at that time.
  </p>
  <p>
    If we begin using AdSense, we will update this policy to reflect the services actually enabled
    on the site and provide any notices or consent controls required by applicable rules. You can
    manage Google ad personalisation through
    <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google My Ad Center</a>.
    You can also learn how
    <a href="https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/7549925?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google AdSense uses cookies</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Affiliate Tracking If We Join Affiliate Programs</h2>
  <p>
    We do not currently use affiliate links. If we later join an affiliate programme, such as CJ
    Affiliate, some links may contain a referral identifier or redirect through the affiliate
    network. When you follow such a link, the network or merchant may use cookies, pixels, or other
    tracking technologies to recognise that a visit or purchase came from our website and to
    attribute any eligible commission to us. These technologies are controlled by the relevant
    third party, not by Bangladesh Travel Guide.
  </p>
  <p>
    If affiliate links are introduced, we will update this policy and our
    <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a> to explain the arrangements in use.
    You can limit tracking through your browser settings and available privacy tools, though doing
    so may prevent an affiliate referral from being attributed.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Managing or Blocking Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Most browsers let you view, block, or delete cookies and manage site data. You can usually find
    these options in the browser's privacy or security settings. Blocking cookies may limit certain
    website functions or prevent analytics and any future advertising or affiliate services from
    working as intended.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics:</strong> You can use the
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google advertising:</strong> If Google ads are shown on this website in the future,
      you can manage ad personalisation through
      <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google My Ad Center</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Browser controls:</strong> Help pages are available for
      <a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chrome</a>,
      <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/kb/enhanced-tracking-protection-firefox-desktop" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firefox</a>,
      and <a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Safari</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Private browsing, tracking protection, and content-blocking tools may also restrict some
    cookies or similar technologies. These tools do not necessarily block every form of tracking.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Third-Party Services and External Websites</h2>
  <p>
    Links on our website may take you to third-party websites. Those websites have their own
    privacy and cookie practices, which we do not control. Please review their policies before
    providing information or using their services.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Cookie Policy when our website, the services we use, or applicable
    requirements change. The “Last updated” date above indicates when this policy was most
    recently revised. If we introduce advertising or affiliate tracking, we will update this page
    to describe the services actually in use.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this Cookie Policy, please contact us through our
    <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
